# Handlers (Fiber)

## Structure

- `index.go`: `{Domain}Handler` + `New{Domain}Handler(...)`
- One HTTP method per file: `registration.go`, `login.go`, `list_widgets.go`
- Alias service import when needed: `userAppService "go-skeleton/internal/services/user_application"`

## Mandatory flow

1. Parse (`BodyParser` / `QueryParser` / `ParamsParser`)
2. `validator.Validate(payload)` — first error only
3. Call service with `c.Context()` — never repo
4. `errors.Respond(c, err)` on failure
5. `api.Base` on success

## Template (matches user_auth/login.go)

```go
func (h *UserAuthHandler) Login(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    payload := new(authentication.Login)
    if err := c.BodyParser(payload); err != nil {
        return errors.Respond(c, errors.From("BAD_REQUEST"))
    }
    if errMessage, err := validator.Validate(payload); err != nil {
        return errors.Respond(c, errors.From("VALIDATION_FAILED").WithDetail(errMessage))
    }
    result, err := h.authenticationService.AuthenticateUser(c.Context(), *payload)
    if err != nil {
        return errors.Respond(c, err)
    }
    return c.Status(fiber.StatusOK).JSON(api.Base{Data: result})
}
```

## Related services in one handler

```go
type UserHandler struct {
    userApplicationService user_application.UserApplicationService
}
```

Only when the HTTP use case spans that service's domain (registration, onboarding, etc.).

## Do / Don't

- DO: validate all inputs; `c.Context()` into services
- DON'T: repos, GORM, business logic, raw error returns
